# Architecture – Online Reservation System

## Architecture Style

Object-Oriented Layered Architecture

The application is divided into separate layers to improve code readability, maintainability, modularity, and future scalability.

Layers:
Presentation Layer
↓
Business Logic Layer
↓
Data Layer

---

## Layer 1 – Presentation Layer (User Interaction)

Purpose:
Responsible for displaying screens and collecting user input.

Responsibilities:

* Display Login Screen
* Display Reservation Form
* Display Cancellation Form
* Show confirmation and error messages

Files:
LoginFrame.java
ReservationFrame.java
CancellationFrame.java

Input:
User Actions

Output:
Validated requests sent to business layer

---

## Layer 2 – Business Logic Layer (Application Processing)

Purpose:
Handle reservation rules and system workflow.

Responsibilities:

* Validate Login
* Generate PNR
* Validate Reservation Inputs
* Process Reservation
* Process Cancellation
* Generate Reservation Summary

Files:
LoginService.java
ReservationService.java
CancellationService.java
TrainService.java

Input:
User Requests

Output:
Processed Reservation Results

---

## Layer 3 – Data Layer (Storage)

Purpose:
Store and retrieve reservation information.

Responsibilities:

* Store Reservations
* Retrieve Reservation Records
* Update Cancellation Status
* Maintain Reservation Data

Files:
ReservationStore.java
reservations.txt

Input:
Processed Data

Output:
Stored Records

---

## Core Project Class

Reservation.java

Purpose:
Represents a single reservation object.

Attributes:

* Passenger Name
* Train Number
* Train Name
* Class Type
* Date of Journey
* Source
* Destination
* PNR
* Reservation Status

Methods:

* generatePNR()
* displayReservation()
* cancelReservation()

---

## Project Workflow

Login
↓
Dashboard
↓
Reservation / Cancellation
↓
Business Processing
↓
Store Data
↓
Display Result



